messages:
sam: Quick flag - noticed the Go and TS SDKs expose different shapes for auth failures in the 'onboarding-getting-started' sample.
priya: what differences?
sam: Go returns a typed error struct: RefreshNeeded{Code:401, Retryable:true, Hint:"refresh token and retry"} and the Type() method returns "RefreshNeeded". TS just throws: Error("401 Unauthorized") from fetch.
ben: that makes automated retry logic messy. Any repro?
sam: yep, repro in sample-app/local-auth-test. Steps: create ephemeral key with 10s TTL, run the client loop. After expiry:
```js
// ts sdk behaviour
try {
  await client.generate(prompt)
} catch (err) {
  // err.message == '401 Unauthorized' -> no easy way to detect refreshable
}
```
```go
// go sdk behaviour
if errors.Is(err, sdk.RefreshNeeded) {
  // has .Retryable true
}
```
maya: For onboarding we should be explicit: sample code must show how to detect and refresh. But better is SDK parity so SDKs map HTTP -> canonical error object.
priya: agree. Proposal: canonical client-side error fields: type (string), status (int), subcode (string, optional), retryable (bool), user_message (string), raw_body (string). Type should be stable: e.g., "Auth.RefreshNeeded".
sam: love it. Also include a small machine-readable hint: hints: ["refresh_token", "backoff:exponential"] so clients can pick strategies.
ben: careful: agents.md wants no nested fields, but this is for SDK contract. For actual messages in Slack keep it simple. I worry about 401 meaning different things - malformed key vs expired. Use subcode like "expired_key" vs "invalid_key".
maya: ops note: auth-service will add an introspection flag next week, might introduce subcodes. We should be robust: SDK should prefer server subcode when present, otherwise synthesize one.
sam: action items I can take: 1) open DEVEX ticket with proposed schema + sample code for TS/Go/Python, 2) update onboarding sample app to assert and log the canonical fields and show a refresh flow, 3) add unit tests in each SDK to assert the shape.
priya: I'll own the docs snippet for the quickstart: show typical retry loop and logging guidance. Include human-friendly copy so new users don't see raw 401.
ben: I'll pick up TS SDK changes and add an adapter layer that normalizes fetch errors into canonical errors. Will try to keep backward compat with a feature flag.
bot-ci: created issue DEVEX-4988: "Canonicalize auth error shape across SDKs + update onboarding sample" (https://github.com/redwood-inference/devex/issues/4988). CI will run a smoke test when PRs land.
sam: thanks. One more ask: telemetry event for uncaught string errors so we can measure how many clients rely on the old text. Add opt-in telemetry in SDKs.
maya: good call. Ops can coordinate deployment windows for auth-service and we can stage SDK releases.
priya: will draft the docs snippet now and post a PR to the sample-app repo.
ben: aiming to open TS PR by EOD, include unit tests and example in README.
sam: great sync. I'll post the DEVEX ticket with the schema + examples for Python/Go/TS. :thumbsup:
